      <li class="rm-index-group">
        <h3 class="rm-index-heading"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/">Comparison of AWS Services</a></h3>
        <p class="rm-index-desc">Head-to-head breakdowns of similar AWS services — the decisions that come up most often in interviews and architecture reviews.</p>
        <ul class="rm-index-subs">
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#database-comparisons">Amazon Aurora vs Amazon RDS</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Aurora is AWS's own cloud-native engine (MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible) with higher throughput and auto-scaling storage; RDS supports more engines including Oracle and SQL Server.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Cognito User Pools vs Identity Pools</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">User Pools handle sign-up/sign-in and issue JWTs; Identity Pools exchange those (or other) identities for temporary AWS credentials.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#storage-comparisons">EFS vs FSx for Windows vs FSx for Lustre</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">EFS is a Linux-native NFS file system; FSx for Windows offers SMB/AD-integrated storage; FSx for Lustre targets high-performance compute and ML workloads.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#compute-comparisons">Amazon EKS vs Amazon ECS</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">EKS runs standard, portable Kubernetes; ECS is AWS's proprietary, simpler orchestrator with tighter native AWS integration.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#streaming--messaging-comparisons">Kinesis Data Streams vs Firehose vs Data Analytics vs Video Streams</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Data Streams gives custom real-time processing control; Firehose auto-delivers to destinations like S3/Redshift; Data Analytics runs SQL/Flink on streams; Video Streams ingests media.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#database-comparisons">Amazon RDS vs DynamoDB</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">RDS is relational with SQL, joins, and ACID transactions; DynamoDB is a serverless NoSQL key-value store optimized for scale and low latency.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#storage-comparisons">Amazon S3 vs EBS vs EFS</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">S3 is object storage accessed over HTTP; EBS is block storage attached to a single EC2 instance; EFS is a shared file system mountable by many instances.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#storage-comparisons">Amazon S3 vs Glacier</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">S3 storage classes suit active and infrequent access; Glacier and Glacier Deep Archive trade retrieval speed for the lowest-cost long-term archival.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#streaming--messaging-comparisons">SWF vs Step Functions vs SQS</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">SWF is legacy workflow orchestration; Step Functions is its modern, visual, serverless successor; SQS is a simple queue, not an orchestrator.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">ALB vs NLB vs CLB</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">ALB operates at Layer 7 for HTTP/gRPC routing; NLB operates at Layer 4 for extreme performance and static IPs; CLB is the legacy load balancer.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">CloudTrail vs CloudWatch</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">CloudTrail logs who did what (API activity for auditing); CloudWatch monitors what's happening (metrics, logs, and alarms for operational health).</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#storage-comparisons">DataSync vs Storage Gateway</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">DataSync performs fast, one-time or scheduled bulk transfers; Storage Gateway provides ongoing, low-latency hybrid access to AWS storage.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Global Accelerator vs CloudFront</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Global Accelerator optimizes network paths for any TCP/UDP application using anycast IPs; CloudFront is a caching CDN for HTTP(S) content.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Secrets Manager vs Systems Manager Parameter Store</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Secrets Manager adds automatic rotation and finer-grained cost per secret; Parameter Store is free (standard tier) and simpler for config values.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Backup &amp; Restore vs Pilot Light vs Warm Standby vs Multi-Site</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Four disaster recovery strategies ordered by increasing cost and decreasing RTO/RPO, from cold backups to fully active multi-region deployments.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">CloudWatch Agent vs SSM Agent vs Custom Daemon Scripts</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">CloudWatch Agent collects OS-level metrics/logs; SSM Agent enables remote management via Systems Manager; custom daemons offer full control at the cost of maintenance.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#storage-comparisons">EBS SSD vs HDD</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">SSD volumes (gp3, io2) suit transactional, IOPS-heavy workloads; HDD volumes (st1, sc1) suit large, sequential, throughput-oriented workloads at lower cost.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#compute-comparisons">ECS vs Lambda</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">ECS runs long-lived, containerized services with full runtime control; Lambda runs short-lived, event-driven functions with zero infrastructure management.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">EC2 vs ELB vs Auto Scaling Health Checks</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">EC2 status checks detect instance/system failures; ELB health checks test app-level responsiveness; ASG combines both to decide when to replace instances.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Elastic Beanstalk vs CloudFormation vs OpsWorks vs CodeDeploy</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Beanstalk is the simplest PaaS abstraction; CloudFormation is full declarative IaC; OpsWorks uses Chef/Puppet; CodeDeploy focuses narrowly on deployment automation.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">ELB Health Checks vs Route 53 Health Checks</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">ELB health checks manage routing within a load balancer's targets; Route 53 health checks control DNS failover across regions or endpoints.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#database-comparisons">Global Secondary Index vs Local Secondary Index</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">GSIs have a different partition key and their own throughput; LSIs share the base table's partition key and must be created at table creation.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Interface Endpoint vs Gateway Endpoint vs Gateway Load Balancer Endpoint</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Interface endpoints use ENIs for most services; Gateway endpoints route via route tables (S3, DynamoDB only, free); GWLB endpoints insert third-party virtual appliances.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Latency vs Geoproximity vs Geolocation Routing</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Latency routing picks the lowest-latency region; Geoproximity routes by geographic distance with bias adjustment; Geolocation routes strictly by user location or compliance needs.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#database-comparisons">Redis Append-Only Files vs Redis Replication</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">AOF persists every write operation to disk for durability; replication copies data to replica nodes for read scaling and failover.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#database-comparisons">Redis Cluster Mode vs Memcached</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Redis Cluster Mode shards data for horizontal scaling with persistence and replication; Memcached is simpler, multi-threaded, but has no persistence.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">S3 Pre-Signed URLs vs CloudFront Signed URLs vs OAI</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Pre-signed URLs grant temporary direct S3 access; CloudFront signed URLs/cookies control access through the CDN; OAI/OAC restricts S3 access to CloudFront only.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/cloud/aws-comparisons/#storage-comparisons">S3 Standard vs Standard-IA vs One Zone-IA</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Standard suits frequently accessed data across 3+ AZs; Standard-IA lowers storage cost for infrequent access; One Zone-IA drops multi-AZ redundancy for the lowest cost.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">S3 Transfer Acceleration vs Direct Connect vs VPN vs Snowball vs Snowmobile</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Ordered roughly by data volume and connectivity needs — from accelerated internet uploads to dedicated lines to physical devices for offline transfer.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Security Group vs NACL</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Security groups are stateful and operate at the instance level; NACLs are stateless and operate as a subnet-level firewall with explicit allow/deny rules.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Service Control Policies vs IAM Policies</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">SCPs set the maximum permissions boundary across an AWS Organization; IAM policies grant actual permissions to users, groups, and roles within an account.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">SNI Custom SSL vs Dedicated IP Custom SSL</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">SNI SSL shares IP addresses across certificates using the SNI TLS extension; Dedicated IP SSL assigns a unique IP per certificate for legacy client support.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">Step Scaling vs Simple Scaling</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Step scaling applies different-sized adjustments based on the magnitude of the alarm breach; simple scaling applies one fixed adjustment per alarm.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label">VPC Interface Endpoint vs Gateway Endpoint</span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Interface endpoints (via PrivateLink/ENI) support most AWS services and cost per hour; Gateway endpoints support only S3 and DynamoDB and are free.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <script type="application/json" id="rm-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(ROADMAP_DATA)}></script>
</StarlightPage>

<style is:global>
  @import "/src/styles/roadmap.css";
</style>

<script>
const ROADMAP = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("rm-data").textContent);

const ICON_PENDING    = `<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6"/></svg>`;
const ICON_INPROGRESS = `<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6"/><polyline points="8 5 8 8 10 10"/></svg>`;
const ICON_DONE       = `<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6"/><polyline points="5.5 8.5 7 10 10.5 6"/></svg>`;
const ICON_ARROW      = `<svg width="20" height="28" viewBox="0 0 20 28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="10" y1="0" x2="10" y2="20"/><polyline points="5 15 10 22 15 15"/></svg>`;
const ICON_CHEVRON    = `<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="3 5 7 9 11 5"/></svg>`;
function iconFor(s: string) { return s==="done"?ICON_DONE:s==="inprogress"?ICON_INPROGRESS:ICON_PENDING; }

const KEY = "aws_roadmap_v1";
function load(): Record<string,string> { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY)||"{}"); } catch { return {}; } }
function save(s: Record<string,string>) { localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(s)); }
let state = load();
let collapsedIds = new Set();
function getS(id: string) { return state[id]||"pending"; }

const FILTER_KEY = "aws_roadmap_filter_v1";
let filterMode = localStorage.getItem(FILTER_KEY) || "de";
function visibleTopics() {
  if (filterMode === "all") return ROADMAP;
  return ROADMAP
    .map(t => ({ ...t, subs: t.subs.filter((s: any) => s.de) }))
    .filter(t => t.subs.length > 0);
}

function allIds() {
  const ids: string[] = [];
  for (const t of ROADMAP) { ids.push(t.id); for (const s of t.subs) ids.push(s.id); }
  return ids;
}

function refreshProgress() {
  const ids = allIds();
  const done = ids.filter(id => getS(id)==="done").length;
  const pct = ids.length ? Math.round((done/ids.length)*100) : 0;
  const bar = document.getElementById("rm-prog-bar");
  const pctEl = document.getElementById("rm-prog-pct");
  if (bar) bar.style.width = `${pct}%`;
  if (pctEl) pctEl.textContent = `${pct}%`;
}

function buildFlow() {
  const flow = document.getElementById("rm-flow");
  if (!flow) return;
  flow.innerHTML = "";
  const topics = visibleTopics();
  topics.forEach((topic, ti) => {
    const s = getS(topic.id);
    const isCollapsed = collapsedIds.has(topic.id);
    const topicEl = document.createElement("div");
    topicEl.className = `rm-topic-node${s!=="pending"?` is-${s}`:""}${isCollapsed?" is-collapsed":""}`;
    topicEl.dataset.id = topic.id;
    topicEl.innerHTML = `<span class="rm-topic-icon">${iconFor(s)}</span><span class="rm-topic-label">${topic.label}</span>${topic.subs.length?`<span class="rm-count-badge">${topic.subs.length}</span>`:""}<span class="rm-chevron">${ICON_CHEVRON}</span>`;
    topicEl.addEventListener("click", () => openPanel(topic.id, "topic"));
    if (topic.subs.length > 0) {
      const chevronEl = topicEl.querySelector(".rm-chevron");
      chevronEl?.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        e.stopPropagation();
        if (collapsedIds.has(topic.id)) collapsedIds.delete(topic.id); else collapsedIds.add(topic.id);
        buildFlow();
      });
    }
    flow.appendChild(topicEl);
    if (topic.subs.length > 0 && !isCollapsed) {
      const group = document.createElement("div");
      group.className = "rm-sub-group";
      for (const sub of topic.subs) {
        const ss = getS(sub.id);
        const subEl = document.createElement("div");
        subEl.className = `rm-sub-node${ss!=="pending"?` is-${ss}`:""}`;
        subEl.dataset.id = sub.id;
        subEl.innerHTML = `<span class="rm-sub-icon">${iconFor(ss)}</span><span class="rm-sub-label">${sub.label}</span>`;
        subEl.addEventListener("click", () => openPanel(sub.id, "subtopic", topic.id));
        group.appendChild(subEl);
      }
      flow.appendChild(group);
    }
    if (ti < topics.length-1) {
      const arrow = document.createElement("div");
      arrow.className = "rm-arrow";
      arrow.innerHTML = ICON_ARROW;
      flow.appendChild(arrow);
    }
  });
}

function updateFilterUI() {
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".rm-filter-btn").forEach(btn => {
    btn.classList.toggle("is-active", btn.dataset.mode === filterMode);
  });
  const total = allIds().length;
  const shown = visibleTopics().reduce((n, t) => n + 1 + t.subs.length, 0);
  const countEl = document.getElementById("rm-filter-count");
  if (countEl) countEl.textContent = `${shown} / ${total} shown`;
}

function setFilterMode(mode: string) {
  if (mode === filterMode) return;
  filterMode = mode;
  localStorage.setItem(FILTER_KEY, mode);
  buildFlow();
  updateFilterUI();
}

let activeId: string|null = null, activeParent: string|null = null;
function findItem(id: string): any {
  for (const t of ROADMAP) { if (t.id===id) return {...t,type:"topic"}; for (const s of t.subs) { if (s.id===id) return {...s,type:"subtopic"}; } }
  return null;
}

function openPanel(id: string, type: string, parentId?: string) {
  activeId = id; activeParent = parentId??null;
  const item = findItem(id); if (!item) return;
  const badge = document.getElementById("rm-panel-badge")!;
  const title = document.getElementById("rm-panel-title")!;
  const body  = document.getElementById("rm-panel-body")!;
  badge.textContent = type==="topic"?"Topic":"Subtopic";
  badge.className   = `rm-panel-badge is-${type}`;
  title.textContent = item.label;
  body.innerHTML    = `<p class="rm-panel-desc">${item.desc}</p>` + (item.link ? `<a href="${item.link}" class="rm-read-more">Read more →</a>` : "");
  if (type==="topic" && item.subs?.length>0) {
    const sublist = document.createElement("div");
    sublist.className = "rm-panel-sublist";
    sublist.innerHTML = `<p class="rm-panel-sublist-title">Subtopics (${item.subs.length})</p>`;
    for (const sub of item.subs) {
      const ss = getS(sub.id);
      const row = document.createElement("div");
      row.className = `rm-panel-subitem${ss!=="pending"?` is-${ss}`:""}`;
      row.dataset.subId = sub.id;
      row.innerHTML = `<span class="rm-panel-subitem-icon">${iconFor(ss)}</span><span class="rm-panel-subitem-label">${sub.label}</span><span class="rm-panel-subitem-tag">${ss}</span>`;
      row.addEventListener("click", e => { e.stopPropagation(); openPanel(sub.id,"subtopic",id); });
      sublist.appendChild(row);
    }
    body.appendChild(sublist);
  }
  syncBtns();
  document.getElementById("rm-drawer")!.classList.add("is-open");
  if (document.body.classList.contains("page-chat-open")) {
    document.body.classList.remove("page-chat-open");
    try { sessionStorage.setItem("page-chat-open", "0"); } catch (_) {}
    document.body.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("page-chat-toggle"));
  }
  document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
}

function closePanel() {
  document.getElementById("rm-drawer")!.classList.remove("is-open");
  document.body.style.overflow = "";
  activeId = activeParent = null;
}

function syncBtns() {
  if (!activeId) return;
  const s = getS(activeId);
  const sel = document.getElementById("rm-status-select") as HTMLSelectElement;
  const dot = document.getElementById("rm-status-dot");
  if (sel) { sel.value = s; sel.className = `rm-status-select${s !== "pending" ? ` is-${s}` : ""}`; }
  if (dot) dot.className = `rm-status-dot${s !== "pending" ? ` is-${s}` : ""}`;
}

function setStatus(id: string, s: string) {
  state[id] = s; save(state); buildFlow(); refreshProgress(); syncBtns();
  const row = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.rm-panel-subitem[data-sub-id="${id}"]`);
  if (row) {
    row.className = `rm-panel-subitem${s!=="pending"?` is-${s}`:""}`;
    row.dataset.subId = id;
    const icon = row.querySelector(".rm-panel-subitem-icon"); const tag = row.querySelector(".rm-panel-subitem-tag");
    if (icon) icon.innerHTML = iconFor(s); if (tag) tag.textContent = s;
  }
}

buildFlow(); refreshProgress(); updateFilterUI();
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".rm-filter-btn").forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener("click", () => setFilterMode(btn.dataset.mode!));
});
document.body.appendChild(document.getElementById("rm-drawer")!);
document.getElementById("rm-panel-close")?.addEventListener("click", closePanel);
document.getElementById("rm-backdrop")?.addEventListener("click", closePanel);
document.addEventListener("keydown", e => { if (e.key==="Escape") closePanel(); });
document.body.addEventListener("page-chat-toggle", () => {
  if (document.body.classList.contains("page-chat-open")) closePanel();
});
document.getElementById("rm-status-select")?.addEventListener("change", (e) => {
  if (activeId) setStatus(activeId, (e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value);
});
</script>
